@page "/about-us" 


<PageTitle>About Us</PageTitle>

<div class="about-hero text-center">
    <span class="about-eyebrow">Track Your Sets</span>
    <h1 class="about-title">Built by programmers, hopefully used by lifters</h1>
    <p class="about-lead">
        Track You Sets started with one idea: Finish the assignment, the second idea how ever was: Logging a workout should be fast and 
        easy, lets be honest your going to pick your phone up on your 1-3min rest why not just track your progress as u do? <br/>
        We're a small team of 3 turning each session into something the consumer can see and feel immediately (as long as we deploy it)
    </p>
</div>

<div class="row g-3 mb-4">
    <div class="col-12 col-md-4">
        <div class="card h-100 value-card">
            <div class="card-body">
                <h5>Focused</h5>
                <p class="card-text text-secondary mb-0">No clutter. just your routines,your sets your numbers</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
    <div class="col-12 col-md-4">
        <div class="card h-100 value-card">
            <div class="card-body">
                <h5>Progress-driven</h5>
                <p class="card-text text-secondary mb-0">Value, reps and trends at a glance so you always know your next move.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
    <div class="col-12 col-md-4">
        <div class="card h-100 value-card">
            <div class="card-body">
                <h5>Fast</h5>
                <p class="card-text text-secondary mb-0">A PWA that uses an API calling exercises for your convenience</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="card team-card mb-4">
    <div class="card-body">
        <div class="text-center mb-4">
            <h2 class="team-heading">Meet the team</h2>
            <p class="text-secondary mb-0">The people building Track Your Sets</p>
        </div>
        <figure class="team-photo mb-0">
            <img src="TheTeam.jpg" alt="The Track Your Sets programming team" class="team-photo-img" loading="lazy"/>
            <figcaption class="team-photo-caption">The Track Your Sets dev crew</figcaption>
        </figure>
    </div>
</div>

<p class="text-center text-secondary about-footnote">Made with heavy lifting and clean commits(almost clean)</p>




